<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Skibbereen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Skibbereen is the largest town in West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cork">Cork</a>, Ireland, on the River Ilen. It grew in the 17th century in a district long held by Gaelic families such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odriscoll">O'Driscolls</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-maccarthy">MacCarthys</a> and O'Donovans. The town and its surroundings suffered some of the worst mortality of the Great Famine of 1845–1852, and its name became a byword for the disaster.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/skibbereen.jpg" alt="Skibbereen" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mike Searle · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Bridge_Skibbereen_-_geograph.org.uk_-_498403.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
